  "verbalization": "Fenofibrate is implicated in the interaction with HPAC through a series of molecular targets, primarily through HepG2 cells. The evidence suggests that fenofibrate acts as a target for multiple compounds, including S-Methylmethionine Sufonium, Diosmetin 7-O-Beta-D-Glucopyranosyl-(1->2)-Beta-D-Glucopyranosyl-(1->2)-[Alpha-L-Rhamnopyranosyl-(1->6)]-Beta-D-Glucopyranoside, and Kaempferol 3-O-D-Galactoside, all of which ultimately target HPAC. These findings indicate that fenofibrate may influence HPAC through a pathway involving HepG2 cells, which are sensitive to these compounds. The integration of these pathways suggests a potential mechanism by which fenofibrate could interact with HPAC, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence supports a role for fenofibrate in modulating HPAC activity via HepG2-mediated pathways, highlighting the importance of HepG2 as a key intermediate in this relationship.",
